  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v2.1.0:\n\t\t\t- Added IEventRequest<Unit> and the built-in Unit response type for fire-and-forget commands\n\t\t\t- Added AddEventOpenBehavior and AddEventBehavior helpers to register pipeline behaviors with registration-time validation\n\t\t\t- Added EventFluxOptions.Timeout to configure the built-in timeout behavior's time limit (previously fixed at 30 seconds)\n\t\t\t- Added AddEventBus<TMarker>() overloads that scan the assembly declaring TMarker\n\t\t\t- Added EventFluxOptions.RequeueStackOnCancellation (opt-in) to requeue undrained stack events on cancellation\n\t\t\t- AddEventBus is now safe to call more than once; discovered handlers are merged instead of re-registering shared services\n\t\t\t- PublishAsync with PublishStrategy.Parallel now aggregates every failing handler's exception into a single AggregateException\n\t\t\t- Deprecated: the EventBus constructors accepting unused assemblies/dictionaryService/eventDictionaryMapService/handlers parameters are now [Obsolete]; resolve IEventBus from DI after AddEventBus() instead. Building with TreatWarningsAsErrors turns direct calls into a build error (CS0618)\n\t\t\t- Aligned the net8.0 target's Microsoft.Extensions.* dependencies to 8.x instead of 9.0.0; a net8 app relying on the 9.x abstractions transitively through EventFlux now resolves 8.x and should reference them directly if 9.x is needed\n\t\t\t- Fixed SendAsync/PublishAsync to throw ArgumentNullException for a null request instead of failing later inside dispatch\n\t\t\t- Performance: added single-handler and synchronous-completion fast paths to PublishAsync; EventDispatcher skips building its pipeline delegate chain when no behaviors are registered",
